         <change when="2016-10-19T06:00:41-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/simoeis">Submit - Line 6: inserted Hagedorn's compelling suggestion to read [ὁρ]μὴν instead of [κώ]μην. The translation should thus be changed to, "We are making this effort of ours for the benefit and continuance of the most sacred treasury" (vel sim.--cf. somewhat different translation of Hagedorn). Line 12f., typo fix, τελέστελέσ --&gt; τελέσ. Line 18: Pap.Choix 27, which is the text that is adopted in this file, prints &lt;Νίλ&gt;ου, even though the papyrus clearly has λίνου. I've reinstated the latter and moved the Pap. Choix reading to the app.</change>
